      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Transitioning to the deterministic Logic-Gate Framework (LGF) will inherently reduce our agility during sudden, non-linear market volatility because rule-based systems lack the adaptive, non-linear inference capabilities of neural architectures. While the LGF offers superior transparency and auditability by strictly adhering to pre-defined logic trees, it risks struggling with unprecedented marketmoving conditions that fall outside the system's existing parameters. Consequently, we would likely need to establish external \"override\" protocols or hybrid layers to ensure compliance intervention thresholds align with extreme volatility scenarios before the Q3 2026 migration.",
